<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Guinea-Bissau junta delays presidential vote for 2 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a86da4b5d7b37a4818ebe20c42e225616b61514583d8eef30fe0f5bdaa893715</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-junta-delays-presidential-vote-for-2-years/a-80068910--e34f489a3b6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-bissau-junta-delays-presidential-vote-for-2-years/a-80068910?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The decision came exactly one year after the military took power on November 26, 2025. The junta said the conditions were insufficient to hold presidential elections for now.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>On farewell trip, Steinmeier calls for more investment in Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:87958ec33f8651ea8245c47c50a0f60ed4e705cd378759fc527150954557b1b1</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717--a2b49bd3f417.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/on-farewell-trip-steinmeier-calls-for-more-investment-in-africa/a-80067717?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cote d'Ivoire, Ghana, Kenya: On his last trip to Africa, outgoing German President Frank-Walter Steinmeier called on companies at home to be bolder and seize opportunities in Africa.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's opposition voices face growing pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a38d561c7e01d65a75b716a28c86cd17504d0ee4e64e0dd3892b653f24c3c911</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:42:34Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-opposition-voices-face-growing-pressure/a-80063893--fc3fb0c33bdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-opposition-voices-face-growing-pressure/a-80063893?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition politicians and government critics say arrests, prosecutions and restrictions on public activity are making it harder to challenge those in power. Is a broader pattern emerging?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt: At least 31 dead after fuel truck overturns on highway</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e45ed5ba8605599773e0d436691b30482df6626af783594131c97e90e813ad56</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T21:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egypt-at-least-31-dead-after-fuel-truck-overturns-on-highway/a-80055175--08e39bb25efc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egypt-at-least-31-dead-after-fuel-truck-overturns-on-highway/a-80055175?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The accident occurred on the packed Ring Road in Giza near Cairo. Dozens of ambulances responded to the crash, and Egyptian health authorities say the death toll could rise.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria detains 5 Mexicans, confiscates over $220 million of meth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05bc3dd25d1fde512ed001fe26639b537f7de6d08b26211e5931ddbe8709496f</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T20:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-detains-5-mexicans-confiscates-over-220-million-of-meth/a-80054606--ed6de81a9556.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-detains-5-mexicans-confiscates-over-220-million-of-meth/a-80054606?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nigeria's anti-drug agency said Mexican experts were allegedly recruited by a Nigerian national to run a meth laboratory in the southeastern state of Enugu.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229044eb65f29fe020e51c060c2c09d06a6ce00955bf9d10d2d64b446e7d10e6</id><updated>2026-11-27T00:41:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
